		{"id":"73f3827cddc0e104","type":"text","text":"Sorting triangles / objects\n\nIf we have a depth buffer, front-to-back sorting can be more efficient.\n\nIf we don't and rely only on the render order, then\n- we must do back-to-front, which may lead to occluded triangles being rendered and then discarded.\n- or we must use a list of colors for each pixel so the color may then be recombined.\n","x":161,"y":-600,"width":250,"height":60},
